# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.14.1
ignore: {}
# The `patch:` entries that used to live here (removed 2026-09, security
# hardening pass) were stale and irrelevant:
#   - They dated from 2019-2020 (SNYK-JS-AXIOS-174505, SNYK-JS-LODASH-450202,
#     SNYK-JS-HTTPSPROXYAGENT-469131, SNYK-JS-LODASH-567746) and targeted CVEs
#     that were fixed upstream years ago.
#   - Almost all of them (`snyk > ... > lodash`, `snyk > ... > graphlib`, ...)
#     referenced the internal dependency tree of the standalone `snyk` CLI
#     tool, which is not a dependency of this project at all (only the
#     unrelated `@snyk/protect` runtime helper is, see package.json). They
#     were most likely auto-generated by `snyk protect` against a globally
#     installed snyk CLI on a contributor's machine and never applied to
#     anything actually shipped by this app.
#   - The one entry that did reference a direct dependency (axios) targeted a
#     pre-0.21 axios SSRF issue; the project now pins a current axios release
#     (see package.json) that is unaffected.
patch: {}
